        <mxCell id="n2" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontColor=#333333;fontStyle=2;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="drift also generates a row class and a companion from each table declaration (Transaction / TransactionsCompanion, and so on). Omitted here by decision &#8212; only hand-written classes get a box. Checked 2026-08-20: drift runs transactions through a method, not a class named Transaction, so the generated row class does not collide." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="110" width="500" x="1220" y="730" as="geometry" />
